## Appendix A Relativistic Calculation

### Rapidity Relation Between Two Reference Frames

Let us consider two inertial reference frames moving with velocity \(\vec{v}\) with respect to each other. Let us also consider a Lorentz boost parallel to the axis \(z\), \(\vec{\beta}=(0,0,\frac{v}{c})\). The relations between the 4-momenta components become:

\[E^{\prime} = \gamma(E-\beta p_{z})\] \[p_{x}^{\prime} = p_{x}\] \[p_{y}^{\prime} = p_{y}\] \[p_{z}^{\prime} = \gamma(p_{z}-\beta E)\] (A.1)

We begin the proof by using \(y=\frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{E+p_{\mbox{\tiny L}}}{E-p_{\mbox{\tiny L}}}\) and considering \(y^{\prime}\) as the rapidity in the moving frame.

_Proof_.

\[y^{\prime} = \frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{E^{\prime}+p_{z}^{\prime}}{E^{\prime}-p_{z}^ {\prime}}\] \[= \frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{\gamma(E-\beta p_{z})+\gamma(p_{z}-\beta E)} {\gamma(E-\beta p_{z})-\gamma(p_{z}-\beta E)}\] \[= \frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{(E+p_{z})(1-\beta)}{(E-p_{z})(1+\beta)}\] \[= \frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{E+p_{z}}{E-p_{z}}+\frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{1- \beta}{1+\beta}\] \[= y+\xi\]Therefore the distribution \(\frac{dN}{dy}\) remains invariant between the relative inertial frames:

\[\frac{dN^{\prime}}{dy}=\frac{dN}{dy}\] (A.2)

### A.2 The Case when \(y\approx\eta\).

Let us begin the proof using the expression \(\eta=-\ln\tan\frac{\theta}{2}\). We shall also consider the case that \(\beta\to 1\), therefore \(E\simeq p\). Let us note that \(\cos\theta=\frac{p_{z}}{p}\) and also the following trigonometric expressions:

\[1+\cos\theta=2\cos^{2}\frac{\theta}{2}\] \[1-\cos\theta=2\sin^{2}\frac{\theta}{2}\]

Proof.: \[y = \frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{E+p_{z}}{1-p_{z}}\] \[= \frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{1+\frac{p_{z}}{E}}{1-\frac{p_{z}}{E}}\] \[\simeq \frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{1+\frac{p_{z}}{p}}{1-\frac{p_{z}}{p}}\] \[= \frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{1+\cos\theta}{1-\cos\theta}\] \[= \frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{\cos^{2}\frac{\theta}{2}}{\sin^{2}\frac{ \theta}{2}}\] \[= \frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{1}{\tan^{2}\frac{\theta}{2}}\] \[= -\ln\tan\frac{\theta}{2}\] \[= \eta\]

